    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm managing a rental property out in Phoenix and the tenant is complaining that one of the bedrooms just isn't getting cold despite the AC running constantly. the rest of the house seems fine. can u give me a list of common reasons why this might be happening so i know what to tell the repair guy?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A single cold room issue in a Phoenix property is a common, yet frustrating, problem. It's often caused by a blockage or weak spot in the airflow, which could be a simple issue like a blocked vent or a damper stuck in the wrong position. More complex issues might involve ductwork leaks or insulation problems specific to that room. You should have your repair guy check the vents, the ductwork leading to that bedroom, and the thermostat's zoning capabilities if you have them.",
