      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While less common, you can't entirely rule out something living in the ductwork, though usually, that would be a more dramatic situation than just weak airflow. A surprisingly large nest of insulation fluff or even a small colony of pests could act as a significant choke point. It's best to start with the simple fixes—checking the damper and looking for obvious debris—before assuming a biological obstruction. A professional inspection is key to distinguishing between a simple stuck flap and a more serious, hidden issue.",
